0,Central-Eastern Niger Fulfulde - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central-Eastern_Niger_Fulfulde,"Central-Eastern Niger Fulfulde, also known as Lettugal Niiser Fulfulde (Ajami: لٜتُّغَلْ نِيسٜرْ فُلْفُلْدٜ) is a variety of the Fula language, a Niger–Congo language predominantly spoken in the Central and Eastern regions of Niger, particularly among the Fulani people.","Fulfulde, Central-Eastern Niger",Niger-Congo
1,Fula language - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fula_language,"Fula dialects are also often split into four regions: the Western area, Central area, Niger and Nigeria, and the Eastern area. [6] The dialects are as follows: Western Area Pulaar Pular Central Area Maasina Fulfulde Gorgal Fulflude Borgu Fulfulde Niger and Nigeria Nigerian Fulfulde (also known as Hausa States Fulani) Niger Lettugal Fulfulde ...","Fulfulde, Central-Eastern Niger",Niger-Congo
2,Central-Eastern Niger Fulfulde — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/central_eastern_niger_fulfulde,"Central-Eastern Niger Fulfulde (ISO 639-3: fuq) is a variety of the Fulfulde language, belonging to the Atlantic branch of the Niger-Congo language family, spoken primarily by the Fulani people in the central-eastern regions of Niger. [1] It encompasses dialects used by both sedentary and semi-sedentary Eastern Fulani (also known as Sokoto Fulani or Fulɓe Siire) communities, who have ...","Fulfulde, Central-Eastern Niger",Niger-Congo
3,"GRN Fulfulde, Central-Eastern Niger: Wodaabe - YouTube",https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL_891CkyN922KlIrbHbwNfHmg0FTpHfLb,"GRN recordings in Fulfulde, Central-Eastern Niger: Wodaabe - Fulfulde, Central-Eastern Niger: Wodaabe These recordings are designed for evangelism and basic Bible teaching to bring the gospel ...","Fulfulde, Central-Eastern Niger",Niger-Congo
4,"Fulfulde, Central-Eastern Niger Language (FUQ) - Ethnologue",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/fuq/,"Central-Eastern Niger Fulfulde is a stable indigenous language of Niger. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family and is part of the Fulah macrolanguage. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Fulfulde, Central-Eastern Niger",Niger-Congo
5,"Fulani - Fulfulde Music, Dicko Fils - Wakati - YouTube Music",https://music.youtube.com/watch?v=nNH7DROc_Fw&list=PLywKu1rCsC-xP292_q719GUclw6FjsmDv,"A Singer blasting kwankwaso for ganduje latest video JADDA GARKO TV 0:00 / 4:03 Fulani - Fulfulde Music, Dicko Fils - Wakati Zone Fulbe Multimedia • 1.4M views • 3.4K likes Start playback","Fulfulde, Central-Eastern Niger",Niger-Congo
6,Central-Eastern Niger Fulfulde Explained,https://everything.explained.today/Central-Eastern_Niger_Fulfulde/,"Central-Eastern Niger Fulfulde, also known as Lettugal Niiser Fulfulde (Ajami: ) is a variety of the Fula language, a Niger–Congo language predominantly spoken in the Central and Eastern regions of Niger, particularly among the Fulani people. The linguistic structure of this language exhibits distinct features, including a Subject-Verb-Object (SVO) word order. Prepositions and postpositions ...","Fulfulde, Central-Eastern Niger",Niger-Congo
7,Fulfulde Media,https://fulfuldemedia.com/en,"Welcome to Fulfulde Media, a collection of free downloadable resources in Fulfulde. You can find radio dramas, music, videos and a complete New Testament. The Fulfulde on this site is mostly from Burkina Faso, although there are also some resources in Maasina Fulfulde (Mali) and Niger Fulfulde. Do get in touch with us if you have questions or comments about the materials on this site. News ...","Fulfulde, Central-Eastern Niger",Niger-Congo
